<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Redland buys into Amcoal tile unit.</title>
<headline>Redland buys into Amcoal tile unit.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Redland Plc of Britain has acquired a one-third stake in Anglo American Coal Corporation's (Amcoal) Coverland Roof Tiles operations for 35 million rand, the South African concern said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>Redland had held a one-third stake in the company until its withdrawal from South Africa in March 1989.</p>
<p>The agreement envisages that Amcoal's Coverland Division will again become a company called Coverland Roof Tiles (Pty) Ltd.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
